      <div type="clause" n="19.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 19.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf se þonne berste, nime þonne leafe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.10"/> ægþer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.11"/> ge heonon ge þanan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.12"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he mote hentan æfter his agenan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.1-2"/> ðonne byrste, nime ðonne leafe ge heonan ge ðeonan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.2"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he mote hæ<hi rend="italic">n</hi>tan æfter is<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.2"/> agan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf se þanne berste, nime þanne geleafe ge heonon ge þanon, þæt he mote hemtan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.1-3"/> æfter his ágenan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="19.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui si fallat, tunc licentiam accipiat, ut abhinc et inde suum audeat perquirere.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="19.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi dies statutus fractus fuerit, accepta<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.6"/> licentia a comitatu in eundo et in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.7"/> redeundo, ut possit accipere náme, quousque habeat sua.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="19.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui si defecerit, accipiat licentiam utrimque et hinc et inde suum (ius) perquirendi.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="19.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="182" ed="#robertson"/>And gyf se<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#IICn_19-2.robnote.fn.14"/> ðonne byrste, nime ðonne leafe ge heonan ge ðeonan þæt he mote hæntan æfter [h]is<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#IICn_19-2.robnote.fn.15"/> agan<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#IICn_19-2.robnote.fn.16"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="262" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gyf se þonne berste, nime þonne leafe ægþer ge heonon ge þanan þæt he mote hentan æfter his agenan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn dieser aber fehlschlägt, dann nehme er Erlaubniss<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.de.1"/>, dass er von hier<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_19-2.lnote.de.2"/> und da [allerseits in Selbsthilfe] hinter seinem Eigenthum her zugreifen dürfe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if that fails, then let him take permission, from here and there [i.e. from both courts], to seize [in self-help] for his own property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="183" ed="#robertson"/>And if this summons fails, he shall get leave, either from the one court or the other<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_19-2.robnote.n.1"/>, to take his own measures for the recovery of his property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="464" ed="#whitelock"/>And if this then fails, he is to get permission either from this court or that,<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_19-2.whinote.n.2"/> that he may seize his own.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="263" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if this proves futile, he shall get permission either here or from the previous court to repossess his property.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_44-2">Leis Wl 44.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘ægþer’ is missing from the other MSS (compare Consiliatio ‘utrimque’). A's ‘hemtan’ for ‘hentan’.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 323, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">defuerit <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">defuerit Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Glosse</hi> Teoþunga <hi rend="italic">Hk; s.u.:</hi> ‘Rechtsbücher 12. Jhs.’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by the gloss Teoþunga Hk; see below: ‘Rechtsbücher 12. Jhs.’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">anddaga <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. eingefügt; vgl. Inst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">anddaga inserted in the 16th cent.; cf. Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">geleafe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">geleafe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt übrigen; vgl.</hi> utrimque <hi rend="italic">Consil.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in the others; cf. utrimque Consil.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þanon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þanon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> sit</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply sit</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Für <hi rend="italic">geleaf</hi> in A gibt Toller zwar das Wort, aber ohne Beleg</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">For <hi rend="italic">geleaf</hi> in A Toller does indeed give the word, but without an instance</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_19-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘überall’ Lambarde, Bigelow <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 19⁴; ‘fern und nahe’ Leis Wl 44; vielleicht ‘hin und her’ meint Inst</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘everywhere’ Lambarde, Bigelow <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 19⁴; ‘far and near’ Leis Wl 44; perhaps Inst means ‘hither and thither’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_19-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">I have taken the phrase <hi rend="italic">ge heonan</hi> etc. to mean either the shire court or the hundred court. Liebermann in his translation (‘von hier und da’) apparently follows Q which has <hi rend="italic">abhinc et inde</hi>; cf. also Leis Wl. 44, 2.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_19-2.robnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">182</biblScope></bibl><label>se</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">anddaga</hi> added in 16th cent. in B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_19-2.robnote.fn.15" n="15" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">182</biblScope></bibl><label>h]is</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">is</hi> B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_19-2.robnote.fn.16" n="16" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">182</biblScope></bibl><label>agan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">agenan</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_19-2.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">464</biblScope></bibl><label>that</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">literally, “hence or thence” which, judging by the order, seems to go with the permission (<hi rend="italic">sic</hi> Miss Robertson), though <hi rend="italic">Quadritpartitus</hi> and Liebermann take it in the next clause, where it would mean that the distraint might be made anywhere on the defaulter’s property.</seg></note>
      </div>
